# Public overlay URLs

Any **content overlay** on the public conference site (abstract details, photo gallery, and future document overlays) must have its own URL so participants can copy/share the link and so browser **Back** / **Forward** / **Escape** close the top layer correctly.

## Do

- Encode the overlay in **query params** on the current edition path (`/` or `/archive/{slug}`), not a separate route that unmounts the page.
- Open with `history.pushState`; change in-overlay position (e.g. gallery slide) with `history.replaceState`; never `router.push` / `router.replace` from `next/navigation` for this — those refetch the RSC tree.
- Keep param names and helpers in `src/utilities/overlayUrl.ts` (`abstract`, `photo`, …). Reuse them; do not invent a second scheme.
- On first load, **sync UI from the URL**. Do not rewrite history on hydrate.
- Close: if `history.state.overlay.pushed` (we used `pushState`), `history.back()`; otherwise `replaceState` to drop the top param so a shared link stays on the edition page.
- Nested overlays are a stack (`?abstract=CODE` then `?abstract=CODE&photo=2`). Back closes the gallery first, then the abstract.
- Prefer a stable public id in the URL (abstract **Code**, then id). 1-based indices for slides.

## Do not

- Open a shareable overlay with `useState` only.
- Give URLs to chrome: **My programme**, install hints, toasts, cookie banners.
- Use hash (`#abstract=`) or parallel `@modal` routes unless the overlay is a real standalone page.

Payload admin screens are exempt (Payload owns those URLs).
